{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_bdrk_01C2V67HF7z4zJ4vGy6bucaS","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-opus-4-7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see the problem. In the test `TestIntegration_RetryPromptsIncludeDebug`, it calls `cm.LoadDebugFromContent(...)` which loads debug info into the parsed `DebugInfo` struct. But now `GenerateDoingPromptFile` uses `contextMgr.GetDebugRaw()` which returns \"\" because `SetDebugRaw` was never called.\n\nSimilarly in `TestGenerateDoingPrompt_WithRetry`, the test loads debug via `cm.LoadDebugFromContent(...)` but the prompt generator now uses `GetDebugRaw()` which returns \"\".\n\nThe fix is: in `GenerateDoingPrompt` and `GenerateDoingPromptFile`, if `GetDebugRaw()` is empty, fall back to `formatDebugContext(contextMgr.GetDebug())`. This preserves backward compatibility with code that still uses `LoadDebugFromContent/LoadDebugFromFile`.\n\n\nI'll implement a fallback mechanism that checks for raw debug context first, then falls back to the parsed format if needed. This way the new code path through runner.go works with `SetDebugRaw`, while the old tests and any existing code using `LoadDebugFromContent` or `LoadDebugFromFile` continue to function properly.","signature":""}],"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9c7b55b1-09d3-48f4-9913-da4bfa9fb3a8","uuid":"56f4ac88-4da1-4b7b-87c4-d7a4ad1d0a4e"}
